However, it's OK to reinvent a wheel that doesn't work properly.
NitroHack's save system is very fragile and frequently results in saves
being lost. NetHack 4's has several features to increase the chances of
saves being recoverable, but they nonetheless seem to need manual
recovery quite a lot.

I'd suggest looking at NitroHack/NetHack 4 for inspiration, but be aware
that the code in question needs rethinking. (In particular, it could
badly do with some sort of specification, rather than all the bits of
the code attempting to cooperate and add together to approximate the
right thing.)

